cmp v20 swallows errors from skip_bytes() in cmp_skip_object, cmp_skip_object_flat, cmp_skip_object_no_limit, cmp_skip_object_limit. Fixed upstream after v20: eeceeea (merged e564b7a, PR #81, 2025). On untrusted input a failed skip can leave the reader at a wrong offset and parsing continues.

Proposal: patches/cmp/ with exactly that upstream fix (plus README with manual re-check), applied at build time; vendored files stay read-only. Alternative: pin a post-v20 master commit instead of v20 — decide in this ticket. Should land before or with the Lua binding ticket.
